From: WEX eDP panel boot-handoff fix
Subject: [PATCH] Display13: admit internal eDP panel through the boot handoff

The Display 13 native path validated the donor's *external* DP/HDMI SST port
object before adopting the firmware boot path:

    if (dp && display13SSTPort(port)) { ... }

display13SSTPort() requires the port's mode field (port+0x550) to be 1 for
DDI 0/1, i.e. an external SST link.  On a Raptor Lake-P laptop the internal
panel is driven by the firmware GOP over the *embedded* DisplayPort link of
the same Combo port, and the firmware leaves port+0x550 == 0.  The strict
check therefore rejected the only valid boot connector, which made
NativeBridge::adoptBootPath() unreachable, left bridge.state.faulted set and
turned wrapDisplay13FramebufferStart() into a hard "No".  IOKit then dropped
AppleIntelFramebufferController, so the accelerator never registered and the
system fell back to the VESA framebuffer.

Measured on hardware (Iris Xe 8086:A7A0, RPL-P, macOS 26.7.1):

    N97FBBootHandoffCheck   all 38 checks pass, check[24] == check[25] == 0
    N97FBPower              STATUS=0 Complete, bootPG/bootDDI protected
    AlderLakeN::dpSource()  17/17 source predicates pass
    N97FBBootHandoff        STATUS=1 NotReady, errors=1, faulted=1, bootPath=0

Fix: keep the strict SST object check for external links, and add a narrowly
scoped relaxation for ports that are confirmed *internal panels*
(adlnOutputWiring.panel bit set).  The relaxed path still requires object
size, DDI identity, memory-owner identity, an unoccupied link and healthy
clock/memory/panel state; the DP source proof and the AUX main-link lease in
adoptDPBootAUX() remain mandatory, as do all NativeBridge::adoptBootPath()
guards.  display13SSTPort() additionally reports the first rejected predicate
so a future failure is a one-line diagnosis instead of a bisect.

---
--- a/WhateverXe/kern_xe.hpp
+++ b/WhateverXe/kern_xe.hpp
@@ -169,7 +169,7 @@
  static bool display13StopTranscoder(void *port);
  static bool display13DeferClock(void *access,uint64_t reg,uint32_t value,uintptr_t caller);
 
- static uint8_t *display13SSTPort(void *port);
+ static uint8_t *display13SSTPort(void *port,uint32_t *reason=nullptr);
  static bool display13HDMIPort(void *port);
  static uint32_t wrapDisplay13TrainingPattern(void *path,uint32_t pattern);
  static uint32_t wrapDisplay13SignalLevels(void *port,uint32_t swing,uint32_t emphasis,void *overrideConfig);

